`Activated` is the button's activation event. `Connect` registers the function that changes `Button.Text`.

Save, check and run. Click **Say hello**. **You should see:** the button change to **Hello, world!**. [Download the finished project]({{Download:First-03-Event}}).

Related reference: [Window](../../api/classes/window/), [TextButton](../../api/classes/textbutton/), [Instance](../../api/globals/instance/) and [UDim2](../../api/globals/udim2/).

## 6. Make a change and return later

Change the greeting, save your file, use **LUI: Stop App**, then **LUI: Run App**. Saving does **not** restart the native app automatically in this preview.

Tomorrow, open the same project folder and run it again. If LUI asks for an SDK, use **LUI: Choose SDK** to select the exact version recorded in `LuiToolchain.json`. Do not edit the pin just to hide a mismatch.

## If something goes wrong

- **No window:** inspect the LUI Preview output and confirm you set `Window.Visible = true`.
- **Old code still running:** stop the native app and run it again after saving.
- **Type error:** read the reported file/line in the Problems panel; compare against the complete checkpoint.
- **SDK missing or mismatched:** keep the extracted SDK together and select the matching installation. See [setup help](../../guides/setup/).

You have made your first LUI app. Next, [build a project library](../advanced-project/) with modules, screens and shared state.
